<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">German–Polish War (1002–1018)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1002">1002</a>–<a href="/years/1018">1018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The German–Polish War of 1002–1018 was a series of conflicts between the Polish duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a> and the German king and emperor Henry II over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. Fighting broke out several times after Bolesław seized the marches in 1002. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen">Peace of Bautzen</a> in 1018 left Lusatia and Milsko in Polish hands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-polish-war-1002-1018.jpg" alt="German–Polish War (1002–1018)" width="320" height="287" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poznaniak, Popik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polska_992_-_1025.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
